faqs:
  - q: "Do you need HubSpot Enterprise for custom objects?"
    a: "Yes. HubSpot's own documentation lists custom objects as an Enterprise feature. If your business tracks something that is not a contact, company, deal or ticket, such as properties, subscriptions or projects, check first whether an existing object or a set of properties can model it before deciding you need Enterprise."
  - q: "Is a HubSpot sandbox included in Professional?"
    a: "No. HubSpot includes a sandbox account with Enterprise editions. On Professional, teams usually test changes on sample records or in a separate test portal, which works but needs more care before changes go live."
  - q: "Can we start on Professional and upgrade later?"
    a: "Yes, and many teams should. Design the data model, lifecycle stages and permissions as if you will grow, so upgrading adds capability on top of a clean structure instead of forcing a rebuild."
  - q: "Which HubSpot tier do your clients usually use?"
    a: "Most of the B2B companies we work with, typically between about 10 and 200 people, are on HubSpot Professional or Enterprise. The common problem is not the tier; it is paying for features the portal was never set up to use."
